    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d717">

                <pb facs="0817" n="807" sameAs="frus:frus1943v01/pg807"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EAC/39</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The First Secretary of the British Embassy</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wright</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Chief of the
                        Division of European Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Matthews</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-11-30">November 30,
                        1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Matthews</hi>: With reference to the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Aide-Mémoire</hi> which I left with you on November
                    19th, I am writing to say that the Soviet Government have now agreed to our
                    suggestions for the Secretariat of the Advisory Council for Europe. They think
                    that the Secretary-General should be elected when the Commission meets.</p>
                <p>As Civil advisers they have appointed A. A. Sobolev,<anchor n="17"
                        xml:id="d717-f1"/> V. S. Kozlov<anchor n="18" xml:id="d717-f2"/> and H. V.
                    Rpanov [<hi rendition="#italic">N. V. Ivanov?</hi>].<anchor n="18"
                        xml:id="d717-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>Yours ever,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Michael Wright</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
